{\sf Lfp}(-,{\sf Set}).\]

\label{l:monoreflection-coslices}
Let ${\sf C}$ be a mono-reflective subcategory of ${\sf D}$ in the category of lfp categories. The following statements hold:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item\label{i:coslice-adj} for any object $c$ of ${\sf C}$, the coslice $c/{\sf C}$ is a mono-reflective subcategory of $c/{\sf D}$ in the category of lfp categories;
\item\label{i:coslice-TM} if ${\sf C}$ has transferable monos, then so does $c/{\sf C}$.
\end{enumerate}
